{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Display LUT}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Display_LUT}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn\tx355 \b\fs36\cf1 Display LUT
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 The \b Display LUT\plain\fs24  is used to perform a translation on the output signal from the image store into Red, Green and Blue signals for the display monitor as defined by the pattern loaded into the LUT.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 The \b user defined pattern\plain\fs24  is a list of points which may be manipulated in the 
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \tab \uldb \b Edit Mode\plain\b\fs24 {\v Edit_Mode}\plain\fs24  
\par 
\par using the \tab \uldb \b Add/Delete Point\plain\b\fs24 {\v Add_Delete_Point}\plain\fs24  and \uldb \b Move Point\plain\b\fs24 {\v Select_Mode}\plain\fs24  functions.
\par 
\par In addition patterns of points may be created using the 
\par 
\par \tab \uldb \b Display LUT Functions\plain\b\fs24 {\v Display_LUT_Functions}\plain\fs24  
\par 
\par \tab \tab  \uldb \b Reset LUT\plain\b\fs24 {\v Reset_LUT}\plain\fs24 , \uldb \b Invert LUT\plain\b\fs24 {\v Invert_LUT},\plain\fs24  \uldb \b Step LUT\plain\b\fs24 {\v Step_LUT}, \uldb Brightness&Contrast\plain\b\fs24 {\v Brightness_Contrast}, \uldb Gamma\plain\b\fs24 {\v Gamma}, \uldb Level\plain\b\fs24 {\v Level_Mode}, \uldb Colour Selection\plain\b\fs24 {\v Colour_Selection} \plain\fs24 and \uldb \b Grey Wedge\plain\b\fs24 {\v Grey_Wedge}.\plain\fs24 
\par 
\par The list of points may be saved with \uldb \b Save LUT As\plain\b\fs24 {\v Save_LUT_As}\plain\fs24  or loaded from file with \uldb \b Open LUT\plain\b\fs24 {\v Open_LUT}\plain\fs24 .
\par \pard\tx355 
\par To reverse false editing steps there is an \uldb \b Undo Function\plain\b\fs24 {\v Undo_Function}\plain\fs24 .
\par 
\par For ease of selecting editing functions a Toolbar can be switched on (\uldb \b Show Toolbar\plain\b\fs24 {\v Show_Toolbar}\plain\fs24 ) or off (\uldb \b Hide Toolbar\plain\b\fs24 {\v Hide_Toolbar}\plain\fs24 ).
\par 
\par \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab \ul Clicking\plain\fs24 {\v CLICK@Leo_1500.HLP} with the right mouse button in the \uldb \b LUT Editor Window\plain\b\fs24 {\v LUT_Editor_Window}\plain\fs24  opens the list with above functions.
\par \page
