{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Edit Mode}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Edit_Mode}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \fs36\cf1 Edit Mode
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par The LUT pattern is represented by a set of lines connecting points.
\par 
\par Each point has as its co-ordinates the input grey level (X in the range 0..255) and the output grey level (Y in the range 0..255).
\par The minimum definition is two points at X=0 and X=255. Other points may be added at other X values, only one point may reside at a specific X value.
\par 
\par In Edit Mode there are two functions available:
\par 
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \b\uldb \tab Add/Delete Point\plain\b\fs24 {\v Add_Delete_Point}\plain\fs24  
\par 
\par and
\par 
\par \{bmc bm31.bmp\}\tab \tab \uldb \b Select Mode\plain\b\fs24 {\v Select_Mode}
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \page
