\par \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\tab \ul Click\plain\fs24 {\v CLICK@SEM.HLP} on the \b Grey Wedge icon\plain\fs24  in the tool bar to activate the function
\par or 
\par 
\par \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab Click in the \uldb \b LUT Editor Window\plain\b\fs24 {\v LUT_Editor_Window}\plain\fs24  with the right button and select from the pop-up menu \b LUT Functions\plain\fs24  and \b Grey Wedge\plain\fs24 .
\par 
\par Grey Wedge is used for setting up and testing LUT data.
\par 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm37.bmp\} This function writes a grey wedge pattern to the image store (0 at the extreme left, 255 at the extreme right) and this destroys any image data present in the image store. 
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \{bmc bm4.bmp\}\tab Note that if the image is not frozen it will be overwritten by the live scan data.
\par 
\par There is \b no\plain\fs24  \uldb \b Undo\plain\b\fs24 {\v Undo_Function}\plain\fs24  option for this function.
