\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Input LUT
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par The \b Input LUT\plain\fs24  is used to perform a translation on the input signal as defined by the pattern loaded into the LUT.
\par 
\par The pattern may be \b transparent\plain\fs24  (no transformation), a \b gamma transformation,\plain\fs24  \b inverted\plain\fs24  or a \b user defined pattern\plain\fs24  created in the Input LUT Window. The pattern is selected in the \b SEM Control Panel \plain\fs24 under \uldb \b SEM Control Detectors\plain\b\fs24 {\v 1WE3854@TabMgr.HLP}\plain\fs24 .
\par 
\par The \b User defined pattern\plain\fs24  is a list of points which may be manipulated in the 
\par \pard 
\par \pard\tx355 \tab \uldb \b Edit Mode\plain\b\fs24 {\v Edit_Mode}\plain\fs24  
\par 
\par using the \tab \uldb \b Add/Delete Point\plain\b\fs24 {\v Add_Delete_Point}\plain\fs24  and \uldb \b Select Mode\plain\b\fs24 {\v Select_Mode}\plain\fs24  functions.
\par 
\par In addition patterns of points may be created using the 
\par 
\par \tab \uldb \b Input LUT Functions\plain\b\fs24 {\v Input_LUT_Functions}\plain\fs24  
\par 
\par \tab \tab  \uldb \b Reset LUT\plain\b\fs24 {\v Reset_LUT}\plain\fs24 , \uldb \b Invert LUT\plain\b\fs24 {\v Invert_LUT} \plain\fs24 and \uldb \b Step LUT\plain\b\fs24 {\v Step_LUT}.\plain\fs24 
\par 
\par The list of points may be saved with \uldb \b Save LUT As\plain\b\fs24 {\v Save_LUT_As}\plain\fs24  or loaded from file with \uldb \b Open LUT\plain\b\fs24 {\v Open_LUT}\plain\fs24 .
\par 
\par To reverse false editing steps there is an \uldb \b Undo Function\plain\b\fs24 {\v Undo_Function}\plain\fs24 .
\par \pard\tx355 
\par For ease of selecting editing functions a Toolbar can be switched on (\uldb \b Show Toolbar\plain\b\fs24 {\v Show_Toolbar}\plain\fs24 ) or off (\uldb \b Hide Toolbar\plain\b\fs24 {\v Hide_Toolbar}\plain\fs24 ).
\par 
\par \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab \ul Clicking\plain\fs24 {\v CLICK@SEM.HLP} with the right mouse button in the \uldb \b LUT Editor Window\plain\b\fs24 {\v LUT_Editor_Window}\plain\fs24  opens the list with above functions.
\par 
