\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Look Up Table Editor Panel
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par The LUT Editor Panel contains an interactive window which allows to set up LUTs in a graphic mode with the aid of the mouse.
\par 
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx7935\cellx8435\cellx12055\pard\intbl The panel is composed of a \uldb \b Menu Bar\plain\b\fs24 {\v Menu_Bar}\plain\fs24  with the menus \uldb \b File\plain\b\fs24 {\v Menu_File}\plain\fs24  and \uldb \b Help\plain\b\fs24 {\v Menu_Help}\plain\fs24  and the \uldb \b Input Window\plain\b\fs24 {\v LUT_Editor_Window}\plain\fs24  for setting up the LUT.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl At the bottom of the panel there is a \b Status Line\plain\fs24  giving feedback about the status of the editor.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl In the \uldb \b Top Window\plain\b\fs24 {\v Top_Window}\plain\fs24  you find the caption of the editor and the control buttons to \b iconise, maximise \plain\fs24 and\b  close\plain\fs24  \{bmc bm46.bmp\} the editor.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl The panel can be \b scaled\plain\fs24  by \ul dragging\plain\fs24 {\v DRAG@SEM.HLP} the edges or the corners with the mouse.\cell\pard \pard\intbl \cell\pard \pard\intbl \{bmc bm40.bmp\}\cell\intbl\row
\pard\tx355 
