\b\fs36\cf1 Top Window
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par The Top Window provides the container in which the other windows reside. 
\par 
\par It contains:
\par \pard\tx355 \tab The Caption bar which displays the icon (1) and the name of the software (2).
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \{bmc bm71.bmp\}
\par \pard\tx355 On the right side of the Caption bar the usual Windows95 buttons are displayed:
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm14.bmp\}\tab The minimize button (3) which enables the application to be iconised.
\par \{bmc bm14.bmp\}\tab The reduce or maximize button (4) to bring back the window to reduced size or full size (for better precision of the input setting).
\par \{bmc bm14.bmp\}\tab The close button (5) to terminate the application.
\par \pard\tx355 \b 
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 Double clicking on the LUT icon \{bmc bm72.bmp\} also terminates the application like the close button (5).
\par \pard\tx355 \b 
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 Underneath the Caption bar the \uldb \b Menu Bar\plain\b\fs24 {\v Menu_Bar}\plain\fs24  is arranged. In the Menu Bar all accessible functions of the LUT Editor software are displayed in the usual drop-down menus.
